    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our undisputed anchor. With a robust 85.93 score, he benefits from a premier matchup against Sugano and an ideal #2 spot in the order, offering the perfect intersection of stolen base upside and favorable SP skill metrics. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier are **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17), both of whom capitalize on high-scoring park factors and a soft matchup against Sugano\u2019s 5.02 xERA. While **Brice Turang** faces a tougher arm in Buehler, his leadoff placement and dynamic platoon advantage keep his efficiency high at 68.98, ensuring our core remains aggressive in the pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who sat on the bubble with a 43.02 score. Ultimately, he was sidelined in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Max Muncy** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom benefit from superior park factors and more advantageous order placement. **McKinstry**\u2019s case was hampered by a poor BvP history and a deep #9 spot, which the optimizer deemed too risky compared to the secondary scoring potential of our active starters. Investors should note that while **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined on the IL, the depth provided by **Austin Riley** and **Jose Caballero** continues to fill the gaps, though **Caballero** owners should watch the plate appearances closely as his 46.23 score is susceptible to his late-order deployment against a difficult arm like Woo. Risks remain across the board as every projected lineup is currently pending, making our daily efficiency scores subject to real-time volatility once the official cards are submitted.",
